<http://data.silknow.org/object/5a209489-79a9-36cc-8bc0-f7a66522e73d/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Plain weave cotton, probably hand woven, embroidered with silk in straight stitches, including satin stitch, pulled thread work; whitework.\nThe top section is dominated by the eye section of a pulled thread net surrounded by bands of needleweaving [a] and a row of 8-pointed stars or flowersheads either side of a narrow pulled thread band, leading into 2 blocks of basketweave stitching either side edged with the needlewoven bands [a].  Along the top a band of separate stylized flowering stems in straight stitch [b].\nThe central oblong section is left undecorated but edged on four sides with [b] edged with pulled thread work, a smaller needlewoven band [c], band [a] then a row of pulled thread lozenges forms infilled with 8-pointed stars/flowerheads, then [c] repeated.\nThe lowest section has a repeating edge of [b], then [a] followed by a row of large touching 8-pointed stars, then [c] and ending with a larger version of [b].\nCotton  thread: no discernable twist\nEmbroidery thread: white silk, 2S"@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/5a209489-79a9-36cc-8bc0-f7a66522e73d> .

<http://data.silknow.org/object/5a209489-79a9-36cc-8bc0-f7a66522e73d>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Middle East, Textile; Face-veil or ruband, white silk-embroidered cotton, Iran, 1800-1860"@en , "Plain weave cotton, probably hand woven, embroidered with silk in straight stitches, including satin stitch, pulled thread work; whitework.\nThe top section is dominated by the eye section of a pulled thread net surrounded by bands of needleweaving [a] and a row of 8-pointed stars or flowersheads either side of a narrow pulled thread band, leading into 2 blocks of basketweave stitching either side edged with the needlewoven bands [a].  Along the top a band of separate stylized flowering stems in straight stitch [b].\nThe central oblong section is left undecorated but edged on four sides with [b] edged with pulled thread work, a smaller needlewoven band [c], band [a] then a row of pulled thread lozenges forms infilled with 8-pointed stars/flowerheads, then [c] repeated.\nThe lowest section has a repeating edge of [b], then [a] followed by a row of large touching 8-pointed stars, then [c] and ending with a larger version of [b].\nCotton  thread: no discernable twist\nEmbroidery thread: white silk, 2S"@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/c8bb47e5-5df5-3cc9-9140-2a9d6de02df1> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/48e40ccf-f294-336f-8c9d-50eb31dc3c6d> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Plain weave cotton, probably hand woven, embroidered with silk in straight stitches, including satin stitch, pulled thread work; whitework.\nThe top section is dominated by the eye section of a pulled thread net surrounded by bands of needleweaving [a] and a row of 8-pointed stars or flowersheads either side of a narrow pulled thread band, leading into 2 blocks of basketweave stitching either side edged with the needlewoven bands [a].  Along the top a band of separate stylized flowering stems in straight stitch [b].\nThe central oblong section is left undecorated but edged on four sides with [b] edged with pulled thread work, a smaller needlewoven band [c], band [a] then a row of pulled thread lozenges forms infilled with 8-pointed stars/flowerheads, then [c] repeated.\nThe lowest section has a repeating edge of [b], then [a] followed by a row of large touching 8-pointed stars, then [c] and ending with a larger version of [b].\nCotton  thread: no discernable twist\nEmbroidery thread: white silk, 2S"@en , "Middle East, Textile; Face-veil or ruband, white silk-embroidered cotton, Iran, 1800-1860"@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/5a209489-79a9-36cc-8bc0-f7a66522e73d/dimension/2> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/5a209489-79a9-36cc-8bc0-f7a66522e73d/dimension/1> ;
